Fixes the fatal error on every bin/magento call with Magento 2.4.9 (symfony/console 7.4):
"Declaration of Wyomind\GoogleProductRatings\Console\Command\Run::execute(...) must be compatible
with Symfony\Component\Console\Command\Command::execute(...): int".

Root cause: symfony/console 7 declares a native int return type on Command::execute(). Run::execute()
overrides it without a return type, so PHP refuses to load the class, and because Magento's
CommandList instantiates every console command at startup, the whole CLI fails, not just this command.
Fix: declare ": int" on Run::execute(). Its only return statement already returns
Cli::RETURN_SUCCESS or Cli::RETURN_FAILURE. Adding the return type is also valid against
symfony/console 6.x, where the parent method has no return type.

Console/Command/Run.php is identical in 3.0.0 and 3.0.5, the only 3.x releases.

